# Findings of gitleaks that are not secrets, one fingerprint per finding, written the way
# gitleaks printed it (F-069, #37, 01.10). gitleaks reads this file from the root of the
# repository, and the check `secrets` stays green only while every finding of the history
# stands here.
#
# Two values are behind the twelve findings, and neither of them is a secret:
#
#   ghs_16…B4a — the token of the example answer of the documentation of GitHub. The hash
#     of it was compared with the example on docs.github.com on 01.10 (F-069). A test of
#     the source of a token hands it to the program under test as the answer of the API,
#     a test of the identity of a run counts it among the secrets of that run, and a test
#     of the redactor takes it out of a text.
#   temp_clone_token — a field of that same example answer, kept as it comes in
#     internal/forge/github/app/testdata/access-token.json.
#
# A fingerprint names the finding and not the value: a placeholder moved or changed by a
# later commit is a new fingerprint, and the check asks about it again. What to do with a
# finding is in README.md.

